(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/html.asl#" :text "Typed HTML: Node (element, text, fragment, raw-text script/style) and Attr (name=value or boolean), a constructor per HTML5 element and the common SVG elements (names that clash with the prelude or with text get El or svg names: mapEl, varEl, objectEl, dataEl, svgText, svgFilter, svgMask, ...), attribute helpers, and a serializer that escapes every text and attribute value, so no caller writes markup in a string.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/html.asl#render" :text "Serializes a Node: text and attribute values escaped; a void element (HTML or SVG) with no children self-closes, br as <br>; script and style bodies are written as text with every </ written <\\/ so they cannot close their element.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/html.asl#button" :text "A button element that is type=button unless the attributes name a type, so a button never submits a form by accident.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/html.asl#style" :text "A style attribute rendered from typed css Decls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/html.asl#styleSheet" :text "A style element whose body is a rendered list of css Rules.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/html.asl#document" :text "html with lang, head and body.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/css.asl#" :text "Styles as data: Decl (plain or !important) and Rule (selector block, an @-block such as media, supports, layer and container, keyframes, font-face, and @-statements such as import and layer order), value helpers (cssVar, px, rem, em, pct, ms, deg, cssString, cssUrl), and minified and pretty renderers.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/markdown.asl#" :text "The Markdown subset documentation uses (headings, fences with a language, tables, - and 1. lists, quotes, rules, code, strong, emphasis and links) parsed into asl-html Nodes; raw HTML in the source stays text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/tests/htmlTest.asl#" :text "Escaping, void and boolean attributes, button type, fragments, script/style bodies that cannot close their element, class/data/aria/style attributes, documents, SVG and the renamed tags.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/tests/cssTest.asl#" :text "Every rule kind minified, pretty output, css string escaping and the value helpers.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/tests/markdownTest.asl#" :text "The Markdown subset: inline spans, headings, lists, fences, tables, emphasis and escaping.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/svg.asl#" :text "Typed SVG drawing for ASL programs: PathCmd (moveTo lineTo hLine vLine curveTo quadTo arcTo close) rendered as path data, shapes with Float64 geometry (canvas rectAt roundRect circleAt ellipseAt lineFrom polylineOf polygonOf pathOf textAt group), transforms, paint attributes, linear gradients and renderSvg, a standalone file with the XML prolog. Numbers print without a trailing .0.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/asnSvg.asl#" :text "ASN drawings to SVG for agents: one (:svg ...) form read with asl-parser/reader; elements by keyword with the aliases rc circ el ln pl poly p txt group; attributes by keyword with the aliases w h v f s sw op sz size t anchor color, camelCase turned kebab-case except SVG's own camelCase names; strings inside text elements become text. An unknown element, an unknown attribute or stray text is an error naming its path in the drawing, never silently kept; width and height without viewBox add one.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/svgCli.asl#" :text "IN=drawing.asn [OUT=drawing.svg] asl-host run asl/packages/asl-html/src/svgCli.asl: converts one ASN drawing, printing the SVG or writing OUT; exit 1 with ERR_SVG lines naming each problem, 2 on a read or write failure or a missing IN.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/tests/svgTest.asl#" :text "Number formatting, path data, shapes, groups and transforms, the XML prolog, an ASN drawing with aliases and camelCase attributes, and the errors for an unknown element, a misspelled attribute, stray text and a non-svg root.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/asn.asl#" :text "Shared reading helpers for the ASN converters: unquote string atoms, keyword and string atom tests, bare names, value text, camelCase to kebab-case, atomOf, headOf, lookup.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/asnHtml.asl#" :text "ASN pages to HTML: elements by HTML5 keyword name, attributes from the global and element attribute lists plus data- and aria- (cls, className, htmlFor and httpEquiv as aliases, camelCase to kebab-case), boolean attributes taking true or false, strings as text (not inside void elements), (:style ...) holding asl-html/asnCss rules and (:svg ...) holding an asl-html/asnSvg drawing. An (:html ...) root renders a document with its doctype; any other root a fragment. Errors name their place.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/asnCss.asl#" :text "ASN stylesheets to CSS: one (:css ...) form of (:rule selector :prop value ...), (:media|:supports|:layer|:container prelude rules...), (:keyframes name (:at stop :prop value ...)...), (:fontFace :prop value ...), (:import url) and (:layerOrder name ...); camelCase properties become kebab-case and --custom properties are kept. An unknown rule, a property without a value or a malformed property name is an error naming its place.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/src/convert.asl#" :text "convertSource kind source for kind svg, html or css; the toolbelt's (:target :name svg|html|css :file F [:out O]) calls it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-html/tests/asnTest.asl#" :text "A page with a style element, boolean attributes, a button and an svg drawing; a fragment; html errors; every css rule kind from ASN; css errors.")
